.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH murk-rotate 1  "rotate " 
.SH NAME
murk\-rotate \- Rotate secrets with new values
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmurk rotate\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-generate\fR] [\fB\-\-length\fR] [\fB\-\-hex\fR] [\fB\-\-values\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-list\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-vault\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIKEY\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rotate secrets with new values
.PP
New values come from a hidden prompt on a terminal, or from piped stdin. With a KEY, murk reads all of stdin as the value. With `\-\-all`, it reads one line per secret, in name order. `\-\-generate` and `\-\-values\-from` supply values another way. murk refuses `\-\-generate` with `\-\-all`.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Rotate all secrets in the vault
.TP
\fB\-\-generate\fR
Generate random values instead of prompting (refused with `\-\-all`)
.TP
\fB\-\-length\fR \fI<LENGTH>\fR [default: 32]
Length in bytes for generated values
.TP
\fB\-\-hex\fR
Encode generated values as hex instead of URL\-safe base64
.TP
\fB\-\-values\-from\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read new values from a dotenv file of KEY=value lines (`\-` for stdin), matched by secret name
.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR
List the secrets that need rotation instead of rotating (exits 1 if any do)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the listing as a JSON object with `verified` and `issues`. The exit code is then 0 even when secrets need rotation
.TP
\fB\-\-vault\fR \fI<VAULT>\fR [default: .murk]
Vault filename
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIKEY\fR]
Secret to rotate. Omit it when you use `\-\-all`
